-- oxy:deploy-phase=pre
--
-- Input-transcription usage unit (@oxy.so/contracts 4.13.0, inference set 3.9.0,
-- mirroring @kaana.ai/contracts 4.1.0): `input_transcription_milliseconds`, the
-- milliseconds of a realtime session's input audio transcribed by the
-- deployment's own transcription model when the provider bills it apart from
-- the session model (Alia ADR 0017). Each ledger table built from
-- `usageUnitColumns()` gains the column, and every CHECK that enumerates the
-- unit vocabulary is re-created with it — exactly as 0127 did for
-- `session_milliseconds`.
--
-- PRE: the arriving image writes every `USAGE_UNIT_COLUMN_KEYS` column, so the
-- column must exist before it serves; the image still serving never names it.
--
-- LOCKING: `ADD COLUMN … DEFAULT 0 NOT NULL` is metadata-only. The re-created
-- CHECKs are `NOT VALID`: each is strictly WIDER than the one it replaces (the
-- new column is 0 on every existing row and the unit lists only gain a member),
-- so no existing row can violate them and no table is scanned under ACCESS
-- EXCLUSIVE inside the migrator's single transaction.
